    "judgment": {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All five mathematical answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-114314: integration by parts with u=x and dv=csc²(x)dx gives -x cot(x)+ln|sin(x)|+C; differentiation cancels the cotangent terms and leaves x csc²(x). q-49674: x cos(2x) is odd, so its integral over the symmetric interval is 0. q-49660: an antiderivative is -(x+1)e^(-x); evaluating from -2 to 0 gives -1-e². q-29742: splitting at x=3 gives -27/2+3/2=-12. q-29734: splitting at x=5 gives -65/2-35/2=-50. The two piecewise-integral answers also agree with the earlier review. No submitted grade was provided; MA evidence comes from the captured worked solutions.",
